/**
\fn pdg::Attributes::setTransform(array number matrix)
\brief Replace the affine transform immediately.

Unlike transform(), replaces the matrix instead of postmultiplying it. AnimatedAttributes adopts it as its shared Animated state and cancels conflicting transform animation. AnimatedAttributes rejects nonfinite or non-affine matrices.

\param matrix Array of nine numbers in column-major order. For a 2D affine transform use [a, b, 0, c, d, 0, tx, ty, 1], mapping (x,y) to (a*x+c*y+tx, b*x+d*y+ty).

\return This object, for chaining.

\par Example
\code{.js}
style.setTransform([1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 20, 10, 1]);
\endcode

\see transform(), getTransform()
*/
